  <section class="setting setting--tint" data-reveal>
    <div class="court">
      <div class="setting__head setting__head--open"><h2>Safeguarding</h2></div>
      <div class="prose" style="max-inline-size:46rem">
        <p>Everyone who works with children or adults at risk here is DBS-checked and trained on a three-year cycle, and two adults are present at every activity. The policy is reviewed annually at a members' meeting, which means the whole church has read it.</p>
        <p>If you are worried about a child or an adult at risk — here or anywhere — contact the safeguarding coordinator directly, or the county team on 0300 123 4043. If someone is in immediate danger, ring 999.</p>
        <p>Concerns about the pastor or any elder should go to the Baptist Union's safeguarding team rather than to the church. You do not need to raise it here first, and you should not feel you have to.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
